><abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.663\">vb.</abbr></b> tremble (Targum Syr.: cf. BH);—<b><abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.491\">Pe</abbr>.</b> <i>Pt.</i> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.505\">pl.</abbr> <span class=\"hebrew\">זָֽאֲעִין</span> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.359\">Kt</abbr>, <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.523\">Qr</abbr> <span class=\"hebrew\">זָֽיְנִין</span>; <span class=\"hebrew\">מִן־קֳדָם</span> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.498\">Pers.</abbr>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"27005019\" data-end-ref=\"27005019\">Dn 5:19</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"27006027\" data-end-ref=\"27006027\">6:27</data>.</p> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">2122</span>]</abbr> † [<span class=\"hebrew\">זִיו</span>] <b>n.m.</b> brightness, splendour (Targum <i>id.,</i> Syr. <span class=\"syriac\">ܙܝܘܐ</span>, perhaps loan-word from <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.17\">As.</abbr> <i>zîmu,</i> chiefly of <i>countenance</i>, Dl<sup>WB</sup> 252: <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.512\">Pr</abbr> 152 <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.450\">Nö<sup>ZMG</sup></abbr> xl (1886), 732 <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.296\">Jen<sup>ZK</sup></abbr> ii. 43 <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.81\">Brock<sup>Lex</sup></abbr>. Syr. 93);—sf. <span class=\"hebrew\">זִיוִי</span> <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"27004033\" data-end-ref=\"27004033\">Dn 4:33</data> <i>splendour</i> of royalty; <span class=\"hebrew\">זִוֵהּ</span> <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"27002031\" data-end-ref=\"27002031\">2:31</data> (of image); <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.505\">pl.</abbr> <i>brightness</i> of countenance: sf. <span class=\"hebrew\">זִיוַי</span> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.359\">Kt</abbr>, <span class=\"hebrew\">זיויך</span> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.359\">Kt</abbr>, <span class=\"hebrew\">זִיוָךְ</span> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.523\">Qr</abbr>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"27005010\" data-end-ref=\"27005010\">5:10</data>, <span class=\"hebrew\">זִי֫וֺהִי</span> <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"27005006\" data-end-ref=\"27005006\">5:6</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"27005009\" data-end-ref=\"27005009\">5:9</data>.</p></blockquote> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">2136,2135</span>]</abbr> † <span class=\"hebrew\">זָכוּ</span> (<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.316\">K<sup>§</sup></abbr> 61, 4) <b>n.f.</b> purity, innocence (cf. BH <span class=\"hebrew\">זָכָה</span>, also Targum <span class=\"hebrew\">דְּכָא</span>, Syr. <span class=\"syriac\">ܕܟܺܝ</span> <i>be clean</i> (<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.454\">Ar.</abbr> <span class=\"arabic\">دَكَاء</span> is <i>be bright</i> (of fire), <i>acute</i> (of mind), <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.326\">etc.)</abbr>, or <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.454\">Ar.</abbr> <span class=\"arabic\">زَكَاء</span>. <i>be pure, good,</i> Targum <span class=\"hebrew\">זְכָא</span>, Syr. <span class=\"syriac\">ܙܟܳܐ</span> <i>be pure, innocent;</i> are these forms with <span class=\"hebrew\">ז</span> secondary? or ancient ‖ ?);—abs. ´<span class=\"hebrew\">ז</span>: <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"27006013\" data-end-ref=\"27006013\">Dn 6:13</data> <i>innocence</i> in God’s sight.</p></blockquote> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">2148</span>]</abbr> † <span class=\"hebrew\">זְכַרְיָה</span> <b>n.pr.m.</b> prophet (BH <i>id.</i>), <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"15005001\" data-end-ref=\"15005001\">Ezr 5:1</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"15006014\" data-end-ref=\"15006014\">6:14</data>.</p></blockquote>",
